DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       If  _s is not NULL, the wwccttoommbb() function converts the wide character _w_c
       to its multibyte representation and stores it at the beginning  of  the
       character  array pointed to by _s.  It updates the shift state, which is
       stored in a static anonymous variable known only to the wwccttoommbb()  func‐
       tion, and returns the length of said multibyte representation, that is,
       the number of bytes written at _s.

       At most MMBB__CCUURR__MMAAXX bytes will be written at _s.  The programmer must en‐
       sure that there is enough room to store the multibyte sequence at _s.

       If  _s is NULL, the wwccttoommbb() function resets the shift state, known only
       to this function, to the initial state, and returns nonzero if the  en‐
       coding  has  nontrivial  shift state, or zero if the encoding is state‐
       less.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       If _s is not NULL, the wwccttoommbb() function returns  the  number  of  bytes
       that have been written to the byte array at _s.  If _w_c can not be repre‐
       sented as a multibyte sequence (according to the current locale), -1 is
       returned.

       If _s is NULL, the wwccttoommbb() function returns nonzero if the encoding has
       nontrivial shift state, or zero if the encoding is stateless.

